{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGqNGVUsvWHJgGBVgQwu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`report.metais` is a template for a **DORA major ICT-related incident report**, the report a financial entity sends its competent authority under Regulation (EU) 2022/2554, using the template from Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/302. It needs three input files in one data directory. Each can be `.json` or `.yaml`.\n\n## 1. `stage`: which report this is\nOne of `\"initial notification\"`, `\"intermediate report\"` or `\"final report\"`. The stage decides which other fields are mandatory.\n\n## 2. `entity`: who is reporting (section 1)\nAlways required:\n- **Submitting entity:** its name and identification code\n- **Affected entity type(s):** for example \"credit institution\" or \"investment firm\", chosen from a fixed list\n- **Primary and second contact:** name and email for each.\n- **Reporting currency:** a 3-letter code such as `EUR`\n\nRequired only in some cases:\n- If the affected entity is not the one submitting, its name and LEI\n- If the entity belongs to a group, the ultimate parent's name and LEI\n\n## 3. `incident`: the incident itself (sections 2–4)\n**Every stage (section 2):**\n- Your internal reference code for the incident. It never changes between reports.\n- When the incident was detected, and when it was classified as major. Times are UTC, written like `2026-03-02T06:40:00Z`.\n- A description of the incident\n- The classification criteria that made it major: clients affected, reputational impact, duration and service downtime, geographical spread, data losses, critical services affected, or economic impact\n- How it was discovered: IT Security, clients, a third-party provider, monitoring systems, and so on\n- Whether the business continuity plan was activated (true or false)\n- If one of the criteria was geographical spread, the affected countries\n- If the incident came from a third-party provider or another financial entity, which one\n\n**From the intermediate report on (section 3):** the impact. That covers when it occurred and when services were restored, how many clients, financial counterparts and transactions were affected (numbers and percentages), duration and downtime (written `DD:HH:MM`), incident type, and the temporary measures taken. More fields become due depending on your answers. For example, a cybersecurity incident also needs the threats and techniques used and indicators of compromise.\n\n**Final report only (section 4):** root cause categories and details, how and when the incident was resolved, gross costs and losses, financial recoveries, and any recurring incidents.\n\n## Running it\n```sh\nmetais sample report.metais --out incident        # optional: starter files filled with generated data\nmetais validate report.metais --data incident     # lists every missing or invalid field at once\nmetais render report.metais --data incident --out report   # produces incident-report.md\n```\n\nKeep one data directory per incident. For each later report, change `stage`, add the fields that stage requires, and correct anything that has changed. The package only writes the report. You still have to file it with your competent authority yourself, in the form and through the channel it requires.\n\nThe package can't check some conditional fields, such as whether the affected entity differs from the submitter or whether transactions were affected; it trusts you to include them when they apply. To see every field's full description, run `metais schema report.metais incident`.\n\nIf you tell me which stage you're on and what you know about the incident, I can draft the input files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7648,"cache_read_input_tokens":26542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7648,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"531d25c6-1996-4e4a-ab1c-0f538ef59990","uuid":"cce77531-6b6f-43d7-9b16-27a47bb321ce","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:53:15.294Z","request_id":"req_011CgGqNGFMJ62owokhpQG55"}
