\nmetais sample report.metais --out incident        # optional: starter files filled with generated data\nmetais validate report.metais --data incident     # lists every missing or invalid field at once\nmetais render report.metais --data incident --out report   # produces incident-report.md\n```\n\nKeep one data directory per incident. For each later report, change `stage`, add the fields that stage requires, and correct anything that has changed. The package only writes the report. You still have to file it with your competent authority yourself, in the form and through the channel it requires.\n\nThe package can't check some conditional fields, such as whether the affected entity differs from the submitter or whether transactions were affected; it trusts you to include them when they apply. To see every field's full description, run `metais schema report.metais incident`.\n\nIf you tell me which stage you're on and what you know about the incident, I can draft the input files.","ttft_ms":2132,"type":"result","duration_ms":21265,"uuid":"f5bec8db-442c-47f3-b0b6-5629b14b0a0e","ttft_stream_ms":1304,"time_to_request_ms":93,"first_content_frame_ms":1304,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
